</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6666FF;" stroke="#6666FF" stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 47.8 0 L 85.57 0"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#6666FF;" fill="#6666FF" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 85.57 0)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.43 0 L -2.66 3.54 L 0 0 L -2.66 -3.54"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#66B3B3;" stroke="#66B3B3" stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 31.69 54.56 L 101.23 18.81"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#66B3B3;" fill="#66B3B3" transform="matrix(0.88936 -0.45721 0.45721 0.88936 101.23 18.81)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.43 0 L -2.66 3.54 L 0 0 L -2.66 -3.54"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFA64D;" stroke="#FFA64D" stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 32 -54.4 L 101.23 -18.81"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFA64D;" fill="#FFA64D" transform="matrix(0.88936 0.45721 -0.45721 0.88936 101.23 -18.81)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.43 0 L -2.66 3.54 L 0 0 L -2.66 -3.54"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D9668C;" stroke="#D9668C"><path style="fill:none" d="M 137.8 -16.79 L 137.8 -38.08"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9668C;" fill="#D9668C" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 137.8 -38.08)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.43 0 L -2.66 3.54 L 0 0 L -2.66 -3.54"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 142.78 -38.25 h 30.83 v 12.06 h -30.83 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D24D79;--ltx-fill-color:#D24D79;" fill="#D24D79" stroke="#D24D79" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 144.16 -36.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.39em;--ltx-fo-height:0.79em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.29)" width="28.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{base}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#D24D79;" mathcolor="#D24D79" mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#D24D79;" mathcolor="#D24D79" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#D24D79;" mathcolor="#D24D79" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#D24D79;" mathcolor="#D24D79" mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#D24D79;" mathcolor="#D24D79" mathsize="0.800em">e</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{base}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF6666;" stroke="#FF6666"><path style="fill:none" d="M 185.59 -59.06 L 223.37 -59.06"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FF6666;" fill="#FF6666" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 223.37 -59.06)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.43 0 L -2.66 3.54 L 0 0 L -2.66 -3.54"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 202.3 -54.07 h 8.79 v 7.69 h -8.79 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#FF4D4D;" fill="#FF4D4D" stroke="#FF4D4D" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 203.68 -52.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.51em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="4.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.92)" width="6.03"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF4D4D;" mathcolor="#FF4D4D" mathsize="0.800em">𝐳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#66FF66;" stroke="#66FF66" stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 323.39 -59.06 L 361.16 -59.06"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#66FF66;" fill="#66FF66" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 361.16 -59.06)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.43 0 L -2.66 3.54 L 0 0 L -2.66 -3.54"></path></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>DynMM-Explain-LLMRec overview: a frozen base aligner fuses CF and text; a tiny online adapter absorbs fresh interactions; a multimodal branch adds vision/audio; soft tokens prompt a frozen LLM; evidence tokens (not shown) ground explanations.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Method: DynMM-Explain-LLMRec</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3 Preliminaries and Overview ‣ Bridging Collaborative Filtering and Large Language Models with Dynamic Alignment, Multimodal Fusion and Evidence-grounded Explanations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for an overview; we detail components below.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Dynamic Incremental Alignment</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We augment the frozen base aligner with a lightweight online adapter <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\Delta}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d_{s}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\Delta}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d_{s}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each item, we produce a dynamic latent</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{z}^{base}_{i}+\alpha_{i}\cdot g_{\Delta}\!\left(\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i},\mathbf{s}_{i}^{\,new}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{z}^{base}_{i}+\alpha_{i}\cdot g_{\Delta}\!\left(\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i},\mathbf{s}_{i}^{\,new}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{i}^{\,new}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{i}^{\,new}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> summarizes recent interactions within a sliding window <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., co-click frequencies, popularity trends), and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}=\sigma(\mathbf{w}^{T}[\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i};\mathbf{s}_{i}^{\,new}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}=\sigma(\mathbf{w}^{T}[\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i};\mathbf{s}_{i}^{\,new}])</annotation></semantics></math> is a learned confidence gate. The adapter <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is a two-layer MLP with ReLU activation: <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\Delta}(\mathbf{x})=\mathbf{W}_{2}\text{ReLU}(\mathbf{W}_{1}\mathbf{x}+\mathbf{b}_{1})+\mathbf{b}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\Delta}(\mathbf{x})=\mathbf{W}_{2}\text{ReLU}(\mathbf{W}_{1}\mathbf{x}+\mathbf{b}_{1})+\mathbf{b}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times(d+d_{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times(d+d_{s})}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. User latents are updated analogously: <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{u}=\mathbf{h}^{base}_{u}+\beta_{u}\cdot g_{\Delta}(\mathbf{r}_{u},\mathbf{s}_{u}^{\,new})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{u}=\mathbf{h}^{base}_{u}+\beta_{u}\cdot g_{\Delta}(\mathbf{r}_{u},\mathbf{s}_{u}^{\,new})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To stabilize updates, we distill the dynamic latent towards the base latent and regularize important parameters using EWC:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{KL}\big(\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z}_{i},\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I})\,\|\,\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z}^{base}_{i},\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{KL}\big(\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z}_{i},\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I})\,\|\,\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z}^{base}_{i},\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{ewc}\,\Omega(\theta_{\Delta})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{ewc}\,\Omega(\theta_{\Delta}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We optimize a sum of ranking, alignment, reconstruction, and stability terms:</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{rank}+\lambda_{m}\,\mathcal{L}_{align}+\lambda_{r}\,\mathcal{L}_{recon}+\lambda_{s}\,\mathcal{L}_{stab}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{rank}+\lambda_{m}\,\mathcal{L}_{align}+\lambda_{r}\,\mathcal{L}_{recon}+\lambda_{s}\,\mathcal{L}_{stab}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{rank}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{rank}</annotation></semantics></math> is cross-entropy or BPR; <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{align}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{align}</annotation></semantics></math> matches CF/text latents; <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{recon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{recon}</annotation></semantics></math> reconstructs CF/text features from <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Online training uses EMA and a small replay buffer.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Multimodal Joint Alignment</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For multimodal items with images or audio, we employ frozen encoders: CLIP ViT-B/32 for visual features <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}^{vis}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{512}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>512</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}^{vis}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{512}</annotation></semantics></math> and Wav2Vec2-Base for audio features <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}^{aud}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{768}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>768</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}^{aud}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{768}</annotation></semantics></math>. A shared projector <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{proj}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{m}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{proj}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{m}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> maps each modality to the joint latent space. We train with a unified contrastive loss across available modalities:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{mm}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{mm}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\;\sum_{(i,j)\in\mathcal{B}}\Big[\mathcal{I}_{cf,txt}(i)\cdot\mathrm{InfoNCE}(\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i},\mathbf{e}^{txt}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>InfoNCE</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\sum_{(i,j)\in\mathcal{B}}\Big[\mathcal{I}_{cf,txt}(i)\cdot\mathrm{InfoNCE}(\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i},\mathbf{e}^{txt}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{I}_{cf,vis}(i)\cdot\mathrm{InfoNCE}(\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i},\mathbf{e}^{vis}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>InfoNCE</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{I}_{cf,vis}(i)\cdot\mathrm{InfoNCE}(\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i},\mathbf{e}^{vis}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{I}_{txt,vis}(i)\cdot\mathrm{InfoNCE}(\mathbf{e}^{txt}_{i},\mathbf{e}^{vis}_{i})\Big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>InfoNCE</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{I}_{txt,vis}(i)\cdot\mathrm{InfoNCE}(\mathbf{e}^{txt}_{i},\mathbf{e}^{vis}_{i})\Big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{m_{1},m_{2}}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{m_{1},m_{2}}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> is an indicator function that equals 1 if both modalities <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1},m_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1},m_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are available for item <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The reconstruction loss is: <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{recon}=\sum_{m\in\{cf,txt,vis,aud\}}\mathcal{I}_{m}(i)\|\hat{\mathbf{e}}^{m}_{i}-\mathbf{e}^{m}_{i}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{recon}=\sum_{m\in\{cf,txt,vis,aud\}}\mathcal{I}_{m}(i)\|\hat{\mathbf{e}}^{m}_{i}-\mathbf{e}^{m}_{i}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{e}}^{m}_{i}=f_{dec}^{(m)}(\mathbf{z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{e}}^{m}_{i}=f_{dec}^{(m)}(\mathbf{z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> are decoded features from the joint latent.</p>
</div>
