<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Evidence-grounded Explainable Generation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For explainable generation, we extract sparse evidence <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{u,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{u,i}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of: (1) Top-<math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> collaborative neighbors: <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{u,i}=\{j\mid\text{sim}(\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i},\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{j})\text{ is top-}k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mtext>sim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{u,i}=\{j\mid\text{sim}(\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{i},\mathbf{e}^{cf}_{j})\text{ is top-}k\}</annotation></semantics></math>; (2) Key attributes from multimodal analysis: <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{u,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{u,i}</annotation></semantics></math> extracted via attention weights over text/visual features. Evidence is encoded into soft tokens <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{e}=f_{evid}(\mathcal{E}_{u,i})\in\mathbb{R}^{E\times d_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{e}=f_{evid}(\mathcal{E}_{u,i})\in\mathbb{R}^{E\times d_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\leq 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\leq 32</annotation></semantics></math> is the evidence length. The multi-task training objective is:</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{exp}=\mathcal{L}_{rank}+\lambda_{e}\,\mathcal{L}_{nlp}+\lambda_{f}\,\mathcal{L}_{faith}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{exp}=\mathcal{L}_{rank}+\lambda_{e}\,\mathcal{L}_{nlp}+\lambda_{f}\,\mathcal{L}_{faith},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{nlp}=-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p(y_{t}|y_{&lt;t},\mathbf{s}_{u},\mathbf{s}_{i},\mathbf{s}_{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{nlp}=-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p(y_{t}|y_{&lt;t},\mathbf{s}_{u},\mathbf{s}_{i},\mathbf{s}_{e})</annotation></semantics></math> is the language modeling loss for generating rationales <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{faith}=\max(0,\text{ACC}(\mathcal{E}_{u,i})-\text{ACC}(\emptyset)-\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>ACC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>ACC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{faith}=\max(0,\text{ACC}(\mathcal{E}_{u,i})-\text{ACC}(\emptyset)-\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> penalizes cases where removing evidence doesn’t hurt performance, with margin <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="S4.F2.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">
<span id="S4.F2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:317.4pt;">
<span id="S4.F2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User history (genres):</span> Sci-Fi, Space, Survival</span>
<span id="S4.F2.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Candidate:</span> The Martian (2015)</span>
<span id="S4.F2.2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evidence:</span> Top neighbors watched Interstellar and Gravity; item shares Sci-Fi attributes.</span>
<span id="S4.F2.2.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rationale (generated):</span> Recommended <em id="S4.F2.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">The Martian</em> because your recent Sci-Fi watches resemble users who also watched it; its ”space survival” attributes match your preferences.</span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Evidence-grounded explanation example.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Soft Prompting and Inference</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">User soft tokens are prepended; candidate soft tokens (joint item latents) are attached to item titles. Evidence tokens are placed in a dedicated segment. All backbones (CF, LLM, vision/audio encoders) are frozen; only small projectors/adapters are learned. Offline, we pre-compute latents and compress with product quantization; online, only <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> updates, keeping latency low.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets.</span> We evaluate on Amazon product datasets with multimodal content: Movies&amp;TV, Video Games, Beauty, and Toys (Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.2 Multimodal Joint Alignment ‣ 4 Method: DynMM-Explain-LLMRec ‣ Bridging Collaborative Filtering and Large Language Models with Dynamic Alignment, Multimodal Fusion and Evidence-grounded Explanations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). We also include KuaiRec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> for short-video recommendation and MovieLens-1M with movie posters. For each dataset, we create: (1) Standard 80/10/10 train/validation/test splits; (2) Cold-start splits where test items have ¡5 interactions; (3) Streaming splits with temporal ordering, using 70% for pre-training and 30% for online evaluation with 1-hour windows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span> We compare against: (1) CF/sequential methods: LightGCN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, S3-Rec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, SGL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>; (2) Multimodal recommenders: MMGCN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, LATTICE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>; (3) LLM-based methods: LLM-only prompting, TALLRec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, A-LLMRec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, RecLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>; (4) Dynamic methods: StreamingRec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>; (5) Explainable methods: NARRE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics.</span> Accuracy: Hit@5/10/20, NDCG@5/10/20, Recall@5/10/20; Efficiency: training time, inference latency, memory usage; Explanation quality: BLEU score with human annotations, faithfulness score via evidence perturbation, consistency score.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation.</span> We use SASRec as the CF backbone with hidden dimension 256. LLM backbones include OPT-1.3B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> and LLaMA-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, both kept frozen. All adapters are two-layer MLPs with hidden dimension 256 and ReLU activation. Visual features use CLIP ViT-B/32 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, audio features use Wav2Vec2-Base <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>. Online updates use replay buffer size 1024 and EMA decay 0.99. Training uses AdamW optimizer with learning rate 1e-3 for adapters and 5e-4 for projectors. All experiments run on NVIDIA A100 GPUs with batch size 256.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Main Results</h3>

