</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DynMM-Explain-LLMRec achieves consistent and statistically significant improvements over static alignment-based LLM recommenders across all datasets. The improvements are driven by: (1) dynamic adapters that capture temporal patterns (+1.2% Hit@10 on Movies&amp;TV); (2) multimodal fusion that enhances cold-item performance (+0.7% Hit@10); and (3) evidence-grounded explanations that improve user trust while maintaining accuracy (+0.5% Hit@10). Statistical significance is confirmed via paired t-tests (p¡0.05) across all metrics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Ablation and Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct comprehensive ablation studies to validate each component’s contribution. All results are averaged over 3 random seeds with different data splits.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Component analysis.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Efficiency analysis. ‣ 5.3 Ablation and Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Bridging Collaborative Filtering and Large Language Models with Dynamic Alignment, Multimodal Fusion and Evidence-grounded Explanations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows that each component contributes meaningfully: dynamic adapters provide the largest gain (+1.2% Hit@10), followed by multimodal fusion (+0.7%) and evidence tokens (+0.5%). The cumulative effect (2.4% improvement) demonstrates the complementary nature of our innovations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Loss function analysis.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Loss function analysis. ‣ 5.3 Ablation and Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Bridging Collaborative Filtering and Large Language Models with Dynamic Alignment, Multimodal Fusion and Evidence-grounded Explanations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows that removing any loss term degrades performance. The stability loss <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math> is crucial for online learning (-0.9% when removed), while the faithfulness loss <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{faith}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{faith}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures explanation quality (-0.8% when removed).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Loss function ablation on Movies&amp;TV. Results show mean ± std over 3 runs.</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Variant</th>
<th id="S5.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Hit@10 (%)</th>
<th id="S5.T3.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">NDCG@10 (%)</th>
<th id="S5.T3.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S5.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> Hit@10</th></tr>
</thead>
